- My girl just caught me.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.960
- So, already we have some problems here.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.860
It appears that Shaggy
and I believe RikRok,

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.720
if that's a real person,

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.320
are in a situation where
one of them has been caught

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:47.120
let's call it red handed and
they need some legal advice.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.050
RikRok is the one who has
gotten himself in trouble

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:52.040
and Shaggy is the reggaeton rapper

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.920
who is providing the counsel here.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.520
Which, in and of itself is a big problem

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.750
because you can't give legal advice

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.040
if you're not an attorney.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.650
Already, Shaggy here has
made some crucial admissions.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:07.780
If I were to represent him, I
think that I would counsel him

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:11.410
not to talk to a random
friend, to talk to a lawyer,

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:14.630
and certainly stop making
admissions against interest

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.500
because if someone got
a hold of this evidence,

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.790
admission against interest
is a hearsay exception.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.180
Shut the (beep) up and
talk to an attorney.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.808
- You let her catch you?

00:02:24.808 --> 00:02:26.660
- I don't know how I left this happen.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:27.770
- With who?
- Okay, ignorance

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:28.803
is not a defense.

00:02:29.876 --> 00:02:30.760
- Nah.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.190
- I don't know what to do.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:33.415
- Say it wasn't you.

00:02:33.415 --> 00:02:34.420
♪ All right. ♪

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.230
- Okay, so this may not
be a strictly legal thing

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.110
that we need to talk about,

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:41.100
but if RikRok is talking
about the girl next door,

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.980
I feel that in a post-R. Kelly world

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.800
we need to question how old this girl is.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.240
Is she past the age of consent?

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.830
I'm not sure I actually want to know

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.100
the answer to this question

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:55.780
because if I know that
there is ongoing criminality

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.660
going on, then I may have an obligation

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:01.200
to turn that over to the police here.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.160
And, speaking of R. Kelly,

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.830
commentators have referred
to R. Kelly's defense

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:11.640
as the Shaggy defense in
his multiple court trials.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.510
- That doesn't even make sense.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:16.077
Why would I hold all these women?

00:03:16.077 --> 00:03:17.302
♪ 'Cause I'm a flirt ♪

00:03:17.302 --> 00:03:20.570
- So, yeah, that's some terrible stuff

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:22.209
to think about as well.

00:03:22.209 --> 00:03:24.279
♪ Honey came in and she
caught me red-handed ♪

00:03:24.279 --> 00:03:27.149
♪ Creepin' with the girl next door ♪

00:03:27.149 --> 00:03:27.982
♪ Picture this ♪

00:03:27.982 --> 00:03:31.282
♪ We were both caught makin'
love on the bathroom floor ♪

00:03:31.282 --> 00:03:34.392
♪ How could I forget that I had ♪

00:03:34.392 --> 00:03:36.170
♪ Given her an extra key ♪

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.920
- Okay, so what my client here has done

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.080
is an admission that's not good.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.400
He has admitted to giving a key

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.480
to the woman who he was cheating on.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.140
Now, that being said,
obviously that cuts against

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.060
any defense of trespass here.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:56.840
But, just because you
have given your girlfriend

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.860
a key to your place
doesn't necessarily mean

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.680
that she has permission
to enter at all times.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.180
Did she enter during
regular business hours?

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:07.800
Did she come over at a time late at night

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.140
when he wouldn't expect her to be there?

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.380
Does she have cohabitation rights

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:15.580
with this particular apartment or house?

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.050
All of these are potential things

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:20.520
that might make it, let's
say, illegal for her

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:25.520
to be trespassing in poor RikRok's house.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.580
She may not have a claim

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.484
to be able to legally
enter into the premises.

00:04:31.484 --> 00:04:34.190
♪ All this time she was standing there ♪

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.400
♪ She never took her eyes off me ♪

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.130
- Okay, we have a problem here.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:41.120
RikRok has admitted
that the only eyewitness

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.370
to this alleged infidelity

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.870
never took her eyes off of the situation.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.100
Now, that's not great.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.050
In general, direct eyewitness testimony

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.070
is not as reliable as you
might necessarily believe.

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:59.170
Often, people forget,
often things are dark,

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.630
and what has been shown
time and time again

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:06.270
is that actual eyewitness
identifications can be suspect.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:10.350
The problem here is that
RikRok has identified

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.850
that this person knew him beforehand.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:16.760
When you have someone who
knows the person in question,

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.100
direct eyewitness testimony
can be very, very good.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.020
But, let's roll the tape back

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:25.062
and take a look at this
supposed eyewitness testimony.

00:05:25.062 --> 00:05:26.065
(tape squeals backwards)

00:05:26.065 --> 00:05:28.670
♪ All this time she was standing there ♪

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:31.070
♪ She never took her eyes off me ♪

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:33.070
- It appears that she never

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.900
got a direct view of this person.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:38.730
She only saw the back of RikRok

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.750
which means that perhaps
this eyewitness testimony

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:45.450
is not quite as damning
as it would first appear.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:48.637
It's entirely plausible that
it, in fact, was not him.

00:05:48.637 --> 00:05:50.490
♪ It wasn't me ♪

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.019
- Except for all the admissions and stuff.

00:05:52.019 --> 00:05:53.878
♪ I even had her in the shower ♪

00:05:53.878 --> 00:05:54.711
♪ It wasn't me ♪

00:05:54.711 --> 00:05:56.630
♪ She even caught me on camera ♪

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:57.990
- So we have a couple of problems here.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:01.490
Number one, this appears
to be security footage

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:05.500
taken from the house itself
which could be a violation

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.060
of the right to privacy if
you were to publicize that.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.730
We've seen all kinds of revenge porn cases

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:14.300
where you can't use this kind of footage

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:17.090
outside of the home itself.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:21.610
Who knows where this poor
woman got this footage from,

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.157
but it may not in fact
be admissible in court

00:06:24.157 --> 00:06:26.650
and it's not clear that
everyone has consented

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:30.930
to the photographs and
photography themselves.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.760
And it's unclear where
this is taking place,

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.990
but if this is in fact in California,

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.410
California is a two-party consent state

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.770
which means that everyone
that is being video recorded

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:43.280
would have to consent to that recording

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.480
being admissible in court

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.599
or to being publicized somewhere else.

00:06:46.599 --> 00:06:49.076
♪ To be a true player
you've to know how to play ♪

00:06:49.076 --> 00:06:51.657
♪ If she say a night
convince her say a day ♪

00:06:51.657 --> 00:06:54.124
♪ Never admit to a word what she say ♪

00:06:54.124 --> 00:06:56.930
♪ And if she claim a yuh,
tell her, baby, no way ♪

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.710
- So, Shaggy is offering the advice

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.500
that you have to convince this woman

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.670
that night is day and that never admit--

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.622
♪ Admit to a word what she say ♪

00:07:06.622 --> 00:07:08.970
- (laughs) We're gonna get
to some other verses here

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:09.830
that are even funnier.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.140
The bottom line is you get the
legal advice that you pay for

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:16.800
and since RikRok has not
paid for this legal advice,

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.750
that is exactly the
value of the legal advice

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.520
that he is getting here.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.290
♪ But she caught me on the counter ♪

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.123
♪ It wasn't me ♪

00:07:23.123 --> 00:07:24.670
♪ Saw me kissin' on the sofa ♪

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:25.571
- Shut up.
♪ It wasn't me ♪

00:07:25.571 --> 00:07:27.320
♪ I even had her in the shower ♪

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:28.153
- Shut up.
♪ It wasn't me ♪

00:07:28.153 --> 00:07:29.969
♪ She even caught me on camera ♪

00:07:29.969 --> 00:07:30.910
♪ It wasn't me ♪

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:34.200
- Some of the best advice
that you can give to a client

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.960
as an attorney is really
just be quiet, stop talking.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.810
Do not talk to the authorities,
don't talk to your friends,

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.560
don't admit any particular
liability or wrongdoing,

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.770
and here RikRok is making
the classic mistake

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:52.470
of not only talking to everyone about it,

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.960
but admitting it over
and over and over again.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:57.010
But, what a competent lawyer will do

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:58.770
is to review all of the evidence.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.850
And once again, I have to point out

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:03.780
that we have never seen RikRok's face

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:05.390
in any of these potential scenes,

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:09.620
so if we can in fact keep his
testimony out of this thing,

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.740
then what we have here is
just circumstantial evidence.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:16.080
Let's see, the counter,
the sofa, the shower,

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:20.010
and also on camera, so four
different potential situations.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:21.760
When you talk about
circumstantial evidence,

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.210
or at least you hear
on TV or in the movies,

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.410
it's always, oh this case is going nowhere

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:27.990
because it's just circumstantial evidence.

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:30.450
This is some really damning
circumstantial evidence.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.680
So the fact that we haven't
seen his face on camera

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:35.870
probably doesn't matter all that much.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:39.370
We've seen a person in RikRok's house

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:42.070
appear to act as if this is their house

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:44.840
and they're having sex all over the place

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:48.630
and, you know, just 'cause
you can't make a positive ID

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.590
doesn't mean that this
circumstantial evidence

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.560
isn't extremely, extremely strong.

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:54.600
And, frankly, in general
circumstantial evidence

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.910
tends to be pretty strong.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.160
DNA evidence is a type of
circumstantial evidence.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.490
So, yeah, RikRok is digging himself

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:04.470
into a deeper and deeper legal hole here.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:05.561
Let's see if he can get out of it.

00:09:05.561 --> 00:09:07.517
♪ She even caught me on camera ♪

00:09:07.517 --> 00:09:08.350
♪ It wasn't me ♪

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:10.096
♪ She saw the marks on my shoulder ♪

00:09:10.096 --> 00:09:11.600
♪ It wasn't me ♪
- Oh no.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.780
- This might have been
the worst verse of all,

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:18.090
if I were trying to defend RikRok here.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.880
Because he mentioned
not only did this woman

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:24.720
see the entire situation, multiple times,

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.610
over and over and over
again, including on camera,

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:31.210
but she also saw the
marks on his shoulder.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.980
Now, why is that legally significant?

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.900
Well, at least in California

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.790
and in most states that I'm aware of,

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.620
part of the discovery process,

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:41.080
which is the pre-trial procedure,

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.960
how you get all of the documents

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:45.040
and various pieces of evidence

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:46.960
that go into the trial itself,

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.880
part of that process involves

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.650
what's called a medical examination.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.320
It's a request for a medical examination.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.153
And so in the same way

00:09:54.153 --> 00:09:57.040
that you can request certain documents,

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.740
in this case you would obviously request

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.320
the video camera footage,

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.770
whether that is in fact admissible or not,

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:05.210
but you can also demand that the court

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:08.690
make an order allowing you
to get the medical records

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:12.770
or, in fact, make a medical
examination of the defendant.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:17.340
And in this case, if there
are marks on his shoulder

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:21.800
from where this other woman
scratched him or bit him,

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:25.780
as I'm told consenting
adults can do on occasion,

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:29.720
the girlfriend or wife could
make a demand of the court

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:33.470
and force RikRok to
stand for an examination

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:36.940
to verify that those
marks are still there.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:39.490
All right, let's address
the elephant in the room.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:43.300
Is Shaggy's recommendation to
claim that, "It wasn't me,"

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.740
over and over and over
again good legal advice?

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.420
- I don't know what to do.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:48.560
- Say it wasn't you.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:49.950
- I'm of two minds about this.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.710
It's obviously not good to go out

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:55.400
and talk about your acts
of infidelity at all.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.890
It'd be better just to shut up.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.490
That being said, as a political defense,

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.540
it might work better than a legal defense.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:04.110
What we have seen, at
least in this day and age,

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:06.810
15 or 20 years after Shaggy pioneered

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.260
the it wasn't me defense
is that some politicians,

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:12.890
who I absolutely won't name,

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:16.100
have been able to use this defense,

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:17.250
let's say, over and over and over again

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:21.000
by doing something and
then either tweeting out

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.300
or having other members

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:24.260
of this particular
political administration

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:27.690
go out and claim that it also wasn't them

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:28.560
and that they didn't do the thing

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:31.080
that they admitted to on
camera or tweeted out.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.630
But anyway, enough about
the (beep) administration.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.730
This is probably not great legal advice

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:37.750
because if, for no other reason,

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:41.780
it cabins you and boxes you
in into one particular story.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.420
Maybe there's an affirmative defense

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:44.875
other than, "It wasn't me."

00:11:44.875 --> 00:11:47.790
(gentle chiming music)

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.940
He tripped and fell into the shower.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:53.690
Or, he moonlights as a yoga instructor

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:56.830
and was just helping this woman,

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:59.890
a private client, obviously,
with her flexibility.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:04.720
And then, having worked up
a sweat in this Bikram yoga

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:08.810
one-on-one session, he offered
the shower to wash off.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:12.780
She, being new to town, didn't
know how to use the shower,

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.310
it's one of those really complicated,

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:16.910
like three handle things,
so he took his shirt off

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:19.862
while he was helping this woman next door.

00:12:19.862 --> 00:12:20.900
♪ It wasn't me ♪

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:23.167
- What I'm saying is that
there are other defenses.

00:12:23.167 --> 00:12:24.870
(stammers) I don't know.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:25.703
I don't know.
(Patrick laughs)

00:12:25.703 --> 00:12:27.621
- [Patrick] This is exceeding
all of my expectations.

00:12:27.621 --> 00:12:30.618
(gentle chiming music)

00:12:30.618 --> 00:12:32.723
♪ Time she was standing there ♪

00:12:32.723 --> 00:12:35.017
♪ She never took her eyes off me ♪

00:12:35.017 --> 00:12:37.438
♪ Wanna tell her that I'm sorry ♪

00:12:37.438 --> 00:12:39.380
♪ For the pain that I've caused ♪

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:40.808
- No, no, no.

00:12:40.808 --> 00:12:42.504
Don't do that.
♪ Listenin' to your reason ♪

00:12:42.504 --> 00:12:45.130
♪ It makes so sense at all ♪

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:46.470
- Absolutely do not do that.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:48.618
Do not admit liability.

00:12:48.618 --> 00:12:51.580
Unless, unless we have
already gone through

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.680
the liability phase, he has been caught,

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.010
he has been found and adjudicated

00:12:56.010 --> 00:13:00.920
to have engaged in this adultery,
then as a last hail Mary,

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.490
perhaps you might be
able to get some clemency

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:05.940
from the judge by admitting culpability

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.690
and taking responsibility
for what you have done.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:11.490
You know, I think that
this particular music video

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.870
is a great example of the fact

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:15.590
that sometimes you don't
get to choose your clients.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:18.240
Sure, it would be great to deal

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:20.060
with innocent people all the time,

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:23.390
but the guilty also require
representation as well,

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:25.570
that's part of what makes
our adversarial system

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.930
work in the first place.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.800
But, you know, if it were up to me,

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.510
I probably would not
choose Shaggy or RikRok

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:35.320
to be my client in this
particular situation.

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:39.460
I think my advice to both
of them would be settle.

